    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always seen math as a tool, not a subject I’m naturally good at. I remember struggling in school, especially with abstract concepts. Now, I use math in daily life—like budgeting or cooking—but I don’t feel confident in advanced topics. It’s practical, not personal. I appreciate how it helps explain patterns in nature, like in chemistry or biology.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, sometimes. When I see complex equations or unfamiliar topics, my mind races. I don’t panic, but I feel a bit overwhelmed. It’s tied to past experiences where I felt judged or failed. I try to reframe it as problem-solving, not perfection. I breathe and break it down. It’s not about being smart—it’s about trying.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used a simple AI app to check my algebra homework. It showed me step-by-step solutions and helped me catch mistakes. It wasn’t perfect—sometimes it skipped steps—but it gave me confidence. I found it useful for quick reviews. I didn’t use it for deep learning, but it helped me feel less alone when stuck.",
